92186272011 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272011 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $det(A)-2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272011 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "51a6e7e0-f39c-5b8c-9665-45f89b4bef77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272011 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain\n\n$$\n|B|=-1\\cdot 1\\cdot 3=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, $det(A)-2det(B)=0-2\\cdot (-3)=6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272013 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272013 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140050" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272013 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272013 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns\n- $A$ has identical columns\n- $A$ has identical rows" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272013 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "14e63fd3-62b7-575e-b489-4cda5c20ed53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272013 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the statements in turn.\n\n- $A$ has proportional columns: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\,✓\n$$\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical columns.\n\n- $A$ does *not* have identical rows.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326938 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186326938 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/